      <div class="msv__faq-list">
        <details>
          <summary>How many months of bank statements do I need for NLV?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Most consulates require 6-12 months. 12 months is the safest choice and shows full-year income consistency. Always check with your specific consulate, but 12 months is the standard.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I use cryptocurrency or digital assets to prove income?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>No. Consulates only accept income documented in traditional bank accounts in fiat currency. Convert crypto to euros/dollars in a bank account, wait for settlement, then document the bank deposits.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I use a joint bank account for the NLV?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Yes, if it's jointly owned (both names on the account) and you can prove legal access. For couples, joint accounts are standard. For shared accounts with family or friends, you must document that you're an authorized user.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What currencies does the consulate accept?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
